<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://ddi-talent.github.io/people/emiliano-videla/eavr.jpg" class="img-fluid quarto-figure quarto-figure-center figure-img"></p>
</figure>
</div>
<p>Hi there! My name is Emiliano and I am part of the DDI Health and Social Care Talent team. My role in the team is as a teaching co-ordinator, supporting course organisers with the delivery of courses, demonstrating tutorials, and contributing with different activities, including the development of this website.</p>
<section id="education" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="education">Education</h2>
<p>I did the equivalent of an integrated master program in biological sciences at the Universidad Nacional de Córdoba, Argentina. I then moved on to a first PhD, at the same university, in biological sciences where, although my main research topic was poultry science and poultry industry, I started my journey in statistical programming.</p>
<p>I started a second PhD working at the University of St.&nbsp;Andrews, in Scotland, and enrolled in a PhD programme at the Universitat de Lleida, Spain, where I specialised myself in the applications of Bayesian networks to understand relationships between the elements of complex systems.</p>
</section>
<section id="latest-articles" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="latest-articles">Latest articles</h2>
<section id="section" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="section">2025</h3>
<p>EA Videla, JM Caliva, PMA Picco, RH Marín, A Luna, FN Nazar (2025). Thymol, Alpha-Tocopherol and Ascorbyl Palmitate as a Natural Feed Supplements to Modulate Immune Variables and Heterophil to Lymphocyte Ratio in Broiler Chickens. Veterinary Medicine and Science. 11(3):e70398</p>


</section>
</section>

